      "rationale": "SCOPING, NOT BLUEPRINT. The real v1.1 blueprint does give IP Services configure-and-verify objectives (4.1 NAT, 4.2 NTP, 4.6 DHCP client and relay, 4.8 SSH), so excluding it here is a Phase 5 effort decision, not a claim about the exam. An earlier version of this file asserted the opposite and was wrong. IP Services hands-on is recorded as backlog: adding it means giving IP Services a non-zero hands-on cell in the N=100 matrix, which changes every domain's draw quota and cascades through the whole allocation. Automation is excluded on a factual basis - 6.5, 6.6 and 6.7 contain no configure-and-verify verb. See docs/GROWTH.md for the IP Services backlog entry.",
